 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "There are, but on the top of a elevation,\nOr on another pinnacle above\nOf some madly building erected location,\nThe rise has been framed in a puzzle\nTo be understood and explained alone,\nThe mystery which is not understood.\nThere is a charm or grace in this unfolding;\nIt has a majesty to be assured\nWhich is not always seen when these appear.\nIt is the work of one man; it appears\nOnly for that very reason; appears\nWhere he may yet see what he interferes.",
